CVE-2026-124709
# openssl / libssl3t64 / openssl-provider-legacy (3.5.7-1~deb13u3, debian 13.7
# trixie): unbounded QUIC RETIRE_CONNECTION_ID backlog DoS (CVE-2026-107494,
# NVD/CNA HIGH 7.5; GitHub GHSA-9x26-7724-x23j auto-scores 9.1 CRITICAL,
# unreviewed; OpenSSL has not published a rating yet). Upstream fix is 3.5.10
# (openssl-3.5 commit 734c6cd7444bdbf589bfec917e47598c1b21ddd3, merged
# 2026-11-22, PR #33544; release scheduled 2026-12-01) but no Debian fix
# exists — bookworm, trixie, trixie-security and unstable all show
# vulnerable/(unfixed) on the Debian security tracker (2026-11-24), and the
# trixie candidate 3.5.9-1~deb13u1 is also vulnerable, so no
# python:3.12-slim digest is CVE-clean. coach-web exposes no QUIC server path
# (python ssl exposes no QUIC API, aioquic not installed), so the vulnerable
# code is unreachable. Re-triage with the base-image block above on
# 2027-01-03; remove once trixie-security ships 3.5.10-1~deb13u1.
# exp: 2027-01-03
